      en: "The Chivor Hydroelectric Plant, also known as the Esmeralda Reservoir, is one of Colombia's most important and iconic energy projects. Located in the Tenza Valley between the departments of Boyacá and Cundinamarca, it utilizes the waters of the Batá River. The facility features an impressive 237-meter high rock-fill dam, which was one of the tallest in the world at the time of its completion in the 1970s. The plant's strategic location in the center of the country allows it to provide essential base-load power to the national grid and the major consumption center of Bogotá. The surrounding landscape is breathtaking, with the deep blue reservoir nestled among steep Andean mountains. Chivor has been a reliable pillar of Colombia's energy system for decades, showcasing the country's early expertise in large-scale dam engineering."
