      en: "The Guavio Hydroelectric Dam is a major power generation facility located in the department of Cundinamarca, approximately 120 kilometers east of Bogotá. It is currently one of the largest hydroelectric plants in operation in Colombia, with an installed capacity of over 1,200 megawatts. The project harnesses the energy of the Guavio River, using a massive rock-fill dam that stands 243 meters high, making it one of the tallest of its kind in the world. The generated power is transmitted via high-voltage lines to the central part of the country, playing a crucial role in meeting the energy needs of the capital region. The plant's underground powerhouse is an engineering marvel, housing large turbines that operate under high pressure. Guavio is a vital asset for the national grid, providing clean and renewable energy that helps balance the country's energy matrix."
